# Internal editorial documents — must never reach the public repo.
# Deliberately a blanket *.docx rule rather than "Revision request*.docx":
#   - no Word document is ever part of the published site (nothing tracked, nothing
#     referenced by content/, templates/ or assets/), so there is nothing to lose;
#   - request documents arrive with inconsistent names ("Revision request_home",
#     "Revision request 1.1 …", "Revision-request …"), and a narrow pattern misses
#     variants;
#   - gitignore matching is only case-insensitive here because macOS sets
#     core.ignorecase=true. On a case-sensitive checkout a narrow pattern would
#     silently stop matching.
# If a .docx ever does belong in the repo, add it explicitly with `git add -f`.
previous_updates/
*.docx
